 :problem
 {:source "owner directive 2026-07-01: more ambitious — bring parts of the hot core (physics solvers, audio mixer) into CLJ/WGSL; re-examine wasmi no-JIT"
  :gap "no authoritative rule for how hot-core compute can move to CLJ/WGSL without breaking the iOS/console wasmi no-JIT invariant; no crate-level ledger distinguishing substrate (stay) from migration targets"
  :risk "porting per-element hot loops into CLJ-WASM silently breaks iOS/console (wasmi interprets every iteration); or the ambition is blocked by treating all Rust as untouchable substrate"}

 :decision
 {:core-rule "the per-element hot loop runs on GPU hardware as WGSL compute; CLJ only authors (edit time) and dispatches (one coarse call per system per frame); the per-element loop never runs in CLJ-WASM"
  :wasmi-resolution "hot loop in WGSL (hardware, not interpreted) + coarse-grained CLJ dispatch (one -tick per system per frame, the existing kami-script-runtime contract) — the no-JIT path is never on the hot loop"
  :ledger-classes
  [:stay-Rust-substrate :migrate-out :port-to-CLJC-domain-interpreter :port-to-WGSL-compute :org-transfer]
  :phases
  {:0 "ledger + guardrails (verify-clj-everywhere WGSL-parity surface; kotoba-boundary-audit --clj-wgsl)"
   :1 "boundary-respecting wins (kotodama migrate-out; data interpreters→CLJC; kami-webgpu fixture single-source; kototama CLJC contract; -clj infra→kotoba-lang org transfer)"
   :2 "ambitious: kami.wgsl @compute support; 5-solver WGSL authored from CLJC (greenfield, reference in kami-genesis); binaural emit :wgsl; postfx→kami.wgsl; ECS defsystem (declare+dispatch, never per-entity)"
   :3 "golden-frame to compute (buffer-hash across wgpu native+web+CPU); clj-wgsl-parity CI workflow; wasmi no-JIT build gate + dispatch-budget test"}
  :out-of-scope
  ["kotoba-crypto (constant-time, #![deny(unsafe_code)])"
   "kotoba-net (libp2p)"
   "kotoba-store/ProllyTree/CID (content-addressed storage hot path)"
   "kotoba-clj + kami-engine-clj (compiler — self-reference)"
   "kotoba-runtime + kami-script-runtime (WASM host = substrate)"
   "kotoba-edn (SSoT EDN reader — porting is circular)"
   "kami-webgpu-rs + kami-render wgpu command recorder (what-to-record → EDN; recorder stays Rust)"
   "kami-genesis Isaac Sim/PhysX facade (vendor API)"
   "hecs ECS storage (60fps tick is native)"
   "aiueos (capability-secure WASM OS supervisor)"]
  :premise-corrections
